```mermaid
%% CHAT SUBMIT + STREAMING + ERROR PROPAGATION
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant UI as Browser UI (ui-2)
  participant Req as UI request() (ui-2/src/api/request.ts)
  participant API as Koa API (api/src/main.ts)
  participant Auth as auth + RBAC (api/src/controller/auth.ts)
  participant Schema as Joi schema (api/src/schemas/index.ts)
  participant Gen as genTask controller (api/src/controller/genTask.ts)
  participant Svc as handleAddGenTask (api/src/service/genTaskService.ts)
  participant DB as DB (gen_task, gen_task_output)
  participant Q as Bull Queue (api/src/queue/queue.ts)
  participant Worker as Worker (api/src/queue/chatGenProcess.ts)
  participant Stream as SSE stream (/api/gen-task-output/stream)

  UI->>Req: POST /api/gen-task {type:"CHAT", formData:{prompt,...}}
  Req->>API: fetch()
  API->>Auth: auth + requireScopedAccess
  alt 401 or 403
    Auth-->>Req: HTTP 401/403 {code,message}
    Req-->>UI: returns {code:401,...} and redirects to "/"
  else allowed
    API->>Schema: validate body (addEditSchema)
    alt 400 invalid payload
      Schema-->>Req: HTTP 400 {code,message}
      Req-->>UI: returns {code:400,message,...}
    else OK
      API->>Gen: getAddMid()
      Gen->>Svc: handleAddGenTask()
      Svc->>DB: INSERT gen_task + gen_task_output (status=QUEUED)
      Svc->>Q: addChatGenTask(job payload)
      alt enqueue failure or overload
        Svc->>DB: mark task/output FAILED (and persist reason)
        Gen-->>Req: HTTP 400 or 429 {code,message}
        Req-->>UI: returns {code:400/429,message,...}
      else enqueued
        Gen-->>Req: HTTP 200 {code:200,result:{taskId,...}}
        Req-->>UI: returns {code:200,result:{taskId,...}}
      end
    end
  end

  UI->>Req: GET /api/gen-task-output/stream?taskId=...&sort=...
  Req->>Stream: open EventSource / fetch stream
  Stream-->>UI: event: status {status:"QUEUED"}

  par worker generates
    Worker->>DB: set output status PROCESSING + write content
    Worker-->>Stream: publish chunk/replace/status/done (Redis pubsub)
    Worker->>DB: terminal status FINISHED or FAILED or CANCEL
  and stream endpoint
    Stream->>DB: poll output row as fallback (when pubsub is quiet)
    Stream-->>UI: event: chunk/replace/status
    alt terminal output
      Stream-->>UI: event: done {status:"FINISHED"|"FAILED"|"CANCEL", content}
    else client disconnect / timeout
      Stream-->>UI: event: timeout or close
    end
  end
```

## Notes

1. Backend error responses are typically produced via `ctx.app.emit('error', { code, message }, ctx)` and handled by `api/src/utils/errHandler.ts`. The handler now accepts either string or numeric `code`/`status` and will use any valid HTTP `4xx/5xx` code (for example `404`) instead of collapsing to `500`.
2. The UI API wrapper `ui-2/src/api/request.ts` returns a normalized `{code, message, ...}` shape and generally does not throw; callers are expected to branch on `code` (and `401` triggers a token clear + redirect to `/`).
